<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Günther I of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1532–1586</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Johann Günther I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Günther I was a count of Schwarzburg and the founder of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sondershausen">Sondershausen</a> line. He ruled the northern Schwarzburg lands from Sondershausen and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnstadt">Arnstadt</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stadtilm">Treaty of Stadtilm</a> of 1599, concluded after his death, confirmed his line's share as the separate county of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-gunther-i-of-schwarzburg-sondershausen.jpg" alt="John Günther I of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gescannt und bearbeitet HieRo GlyPhe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_G%C3%BCnther.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
